                    Part Time Remote Position – Philippines



About the Role



We are looking for a practical, organised person to help manage online customer engagement and travel content for a busy Canary Islands excursion and tourism business.



This is not a “social media manager” role where you just post nice pictures or say you know how to use
.



This is a hands-on role involving customer comments, lead generation, website content, AI-assisted blogs, travel news updates, and helping turn online attention into real bookings.



Main Responsibilities

Customer Comments & Engagement



You will monitor comments and replies across our social media channels and make sure customers are answered properly.



This includes:



replying to comments on videos and posts;

acknowledging customer questions;

spotting sales opportunities;

encouraging people to message us when they need help;

responding naturally, not like a robot;

passing real booking enquiries into the correct system or team;

making sure no good lead is ignored.

Example



If someone comments, “We are coming to Lanzarote next week,” we do not just like the comment.



We reply properly, for example:



"Brilliant, you’ll have a great time. Send us a message and we can help you with the best excursions for your dates."



The aim is to turn comments into conversations and conversations into bookings.



Content Support



You will also help create useful travel content for our website and social platforms.



You do not need to be a professional writer. We use AI tools to help with research and writing.



However, you must be able to:



research topics properly;

use AI tools sensibly;

check that the information makes sense;

edit content so it sounds natural;

upload blogs, news updates and guides to our system;

follow instructions and templates;

keep content organised and consistent.

Examples of content you may help create:

weekly Canary Islands travel news updates;

Lanzarote excursion guides;

"Best things to do in Lanzarote this week" articles;

car hire advice;

airport transfer information;

family holiday tips;

restaurant and local business features;

simple website blogs designed to help customers and generate enquiries.

AI-Assisted Work



We are not looking for someone to manually write everything from scratch.



We are looking for someone who can use AI properly.



You may be asked to use AI to:



research the latest travel news;

create first drafts of blogs;

rewrite content in a better tone;

produce short captions;

summarise information;

create FAQs;

prepare website content;

help turn customer questions into useful content ideas.



You must be comfortable learning how to prompt AI tools and then checking, editing and uploading the final result.



AI will help produce the content, but you are responsible for making sure it is useful, accurate, clear and suitable for our customers.



The Person We Want



We are looking for someone who is:



organised;

reliable;

practical;

good with written English;

comfortable using online tools;

willing to learn;

good at following systems;

able to spot a customer enquiry;

not afraid to reply to people;

able to work quickly without needing constant supervision.



You do not need to be a designer, influencer or professional social media expert.



You do need to be consistent, switched on and able to understand when a comment is a possible customer.



Useful Skills



Experience with any of the following would be useful, but not essential:



 pages and groups;

Instagram comments and messages;

YouTube comments;

TikTok comments;

WordPress or website uploads;

Canva;

ChatGPT or other AI tools;

basic blog formatting;

customer service;

travel or tourism;

CRM systems;

GoHighLevel;

ManyChat.



Training will be provided where needed.



What This Role Is Not



This role is not for someone who only wants to:



create pretty posts;

call themselves a social media manager;

build a personal brand;

spend all day scrolling;

post random content with no purpose;

use
 but not deal with customers;

avoid admin work.



This is a working role inside a busy tourism business.



You will be expected to help with comments, leads, content, website updates and customer engagement.



What Success Looks Like



You will be successful in this role if:



customer comments are answered quickly and naturally;

booking opportunities are spotted and passed on;

social media feels active and human, not robotic;

useful website content is created every week;

blogs and news updates are uploaded correctly;

fewer leads are missed;

the team can trust you to manage daily engagement without being chased.

Application Task



To apply, please do not send a long generic CV about being a social media manager.



Instead, please answer these questions:



Have you ever replied to customer comments or messages for a business before?

Are you comfortable using AI tools such as ChatGPT to help create content?

Can you upload and format website articles or are you willing to learn?



What would you reply if someone commented on a Lanzarote video saying:



"We arrive next week, what should we book?"



Write three simple blog ideas for a Lanzarote excursion website.



We are looking for someone practical, reliable and willing to learn.



The right person will be trained into our systems and become an important part of our customer engagement and content process.

                    Intake Specialist – Estate Planning and Financial Services



We are seeking a highly organized and client-focused Intake Specialist to support a U.S.-based estate-planning and financial-planning practice. The ideal candidate will have experience communicating with prospective clients, managing intake workflows, maintaining CRM records, and handling sensitive legal and financial information professionally.



Key Responsibilities

Respond promptly and professionally to prospective and existing clients.

Conduct initial intake calls and gather relevant personal, legal, and financial information.

Schedule consultations and follow up with prospective clients.

Maintain accurate client records, notes, documents, and follow-up tasks in the firm’s CRM.

Assist with onboarding, engagement documents, and coordination between the financial-planning and legal teams.

Track leads and matters through each stage of the intake process.

Communicate complex information clearly, warmly, and professionally.

Protect client confidentiality and handle sensitive information with discretion.



Preferred Qualifications

Candidates should possess one or more of the following:

Estate-planning intake experience;

At least three years of financial-services experience;

Experience working with a U.S.-based financial-services company;

Strong knowledge of financial terminology;

Paralegal or legal-assistant experience;

A Philippine Juris Doctor degree; or

Strong CRM, client-communication, and relationship-management skills.

Additional Requirements

Excellent written and spoken English;

Strong attention to detail and follow-through;

Ability to manage multiple leads, deadlines, and client communications;

Professional, empathetic, and confident telephone manner;

Proficiency with cloud-based systems and willingness to learn new legal and financial-planning software;

Reliable internet connection and a suitable remote-work environment; and

Availability during designated U.S. business hours.



